 [Satisfies supervisor comment #1 — explicit RDP formula + Theorem 1]\n#\n# ==========================================================================\n#  PRIVACY ANALYSIS SUBSECTION\n# ==========================================================================\n#\n# We use Rényi Differential Privacy (RDP) composition (Mironov, 2017).\n#\n# Definition (RDP): A randomised mechanism M satisfies (α, ε_α)-RDP if\n# for all neighbouring datasets x, x' differing in one sample:\n#\n#   D_α( M(x) || M(x') ) ≤ ε_α\n#\n# where D_α is the Rényi divergence of order α > 1.\n#\n# Per-step RDP for subsampled Gaussian mechanism (Mironov 2017, Thm 3):\n# With noise multiplier σ and sampling rate q = batch_size / n:\n#\n#   ε_RDP(α) ≈  α · q²  /  (2σ²)       [simplified; Opacus uses exact form]\n#\n# Sequential composition across T steps:\n#\n#   ε_RDP_total(α)  =  T · ε_RDP_per_step(α)\n#\n# Converting RDP → (ε, δ)-DP  (Balle et al., 2020):\n#\n#   ε(δ) = min_{α > 1}  [ ε_RDP(α)  +  log(1 - 1/α) - log(δ · (α-1)/α) ]\n#                                        ────────────────────────────────\n#                                           (α - 1)\n#\n# Applied to FedAdaPriv-CPU (sequential composition across phases):\n#\n#   Phase 1 (warmstart):  T_ws   = WARMSTART_ROUNDS × E × ⌊n/b⌋\n#                         budget : ε_warmstart = 1.0\n#\n#   Phase 2 (main FL):    T_main = NUM_ROUNDS × E_actual × ⌊n/b⌋\n#                         budget : ε_main      = 2.0\n#\n#   W_k,r leakage:        Laplace(Δf=1.0, ε_weight=0.5) per round\n#                         parallel composition → max(ε_main, ε_weight) = 2.0\n#                         (does NOT increase total)\n#\n#   Sequential total:     ε_total = ε_warmstart + ε_main = 1.0 + 2.0 = 3.0\n#\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Theorem 1 (FedAdaPriv-CPU):\n#   FedAdaPriv-CPU satisfies (3.0, 1e-5)-DP at the sample level for each\n#   client, composed across all training phases via the RDP accountant.\n#